Oliver Day is a Nephilim of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]]'s research department, red-skinned and horned, with goat's eyes and hooves. He was aboard the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]] when it struck the ascending [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]], and the collision shut him inside a shelter on the ship's bridge floor, where he has lived some thirty years on berries he grows by magic.

He knows the wreck's workings. Every shelter but his own stayed sealed on the inside, and the sealed rooms open to a key cut in Sedecium's sixteen-pointed star. The great door at the foot of the elevator shaft is a one-way passage into the engine room, and the magic that fills it can be passed only by a body falling from high enough under a rite of heat-shielding, such as Oliver can cast. He is of the research staff, no captain, and cannot steer the ship. His own piece of the star-key he left behind in his office in the dormitory.
